<section class="section">
  <div class="container text-center" style="max-width:720px">
    <span class="section-label">Process FAQ</span>
    <h2 class="section-title" style="margin-inline:auto">Common process questions.</h2>
    <div class="faq-list">
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">What if I don't have content yet? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">We write it. After the discovery call we draft copy in your voice from what you told us, send it for review, and revise until it reads the way you'd actually talk to a customer.</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">Can I see the site while you're building it? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Yes; we share a live preview link usually within 3&ndash;5 business days. You can forward it to anyone whose opinion you want. You stay in the loop the whole time.</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">How many rounds of revisions do I get? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Unlimited. We don't charge by the change and we don't rush you. We want you to be happy with it before launch; not after.</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">What if I already have a domain? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Perfect. We'll handle the DNS switch on launch day. You keep the domain in your name; we just point it at our hosting.</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">What happens to my old website? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">We coordinate the cut-over so there's no downtime. Once the new site is live, you can take down the old one or keep it archived; your choice.</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
